<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>An irrigation channel at Mwea is <m>{2}</m> m wide. Its depth at a distance <m>x</m> m from one side is <m>d = {\frac{3}{4}}x({2} - x)</m> m. An engineer estimates the area of the cross-section with the mid-ordinate rule and <m>{4}</m> strips.</p><p>(a) Find the engineer's estimate, correct to 3 decimal places.</p><div>Estimate <m>=</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/> <m>\text{m}^2</m>  </div><p>(b) Find the exact area of the cross-section. Give the exact value.</p><div>Exact area <m>=</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/> <m>\text{m}^2</m>  </div><p>(c) Find the percentage error of the estimate, correct to 2 decimal places. Do not round your estimate before this part.</p><div>Percentage error <m>=</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/> %  </div><p>(d) Is the estimate within <m>1\%</m> of the exact area?</p><div>[ Yes | No ]  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The mid-ordinate rule uses the depth at the middle of each strip. Here the strips have width <m>h = {2} \div {4} = {0.5}</m> m.</p><p>(a) The middles of the strips are at <m>x = {\left[ 0.25 , 0.75 , 1.25 , 1.75 \right]}</m>, where the depths are <m>{\left[ 0.328125 , 0.703125 , 0.703125 , 0.328125 \right]}</m>. So the estimate is <m>{0.5} \times {2.062} = {1.03125} \approx {1.031}</m> <m>\text{m}^2</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>\displaystyle \int_0^{ {2} } {\frac{3}{4}}x({2} - x)\,dx = \left[{-\frac{x^3-3 x^2}{4}}\right]_0^{ {2} } = {1}</m> <m>\text{m}^2</m>.</p><p>(c) Percentage error <m>= \dfrac{ {0.03125} }{ {1} } \times 100 = {3.125} \approx {3.13}\,\%</m>.</p><p>(d) No: the percentage error is more than <m>1\%</m>.</p><p>For every curve of this shape the percentage error is <m>50 \div n^2</m> with <m>n</m> strips, whatever the size of the channel.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{33}{32}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{25}{8}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p>No</p></answer>
</stack-static>